{
"My uncle works in a shoe factory.": "62939f12ae05",
"Name two things in a fab that use a lot of electricity.": "35d86fc0e207",
"Now the electricity. Chips are made in a cleanroom, where fans in the ceiling push air down through very fine filters, and the air is used again and again. The temperature and humidity are tightly controlled as well. Ordinary city air holds about 35 million particles in every cubic meter. The air in a cleanroom may hold a few thousand, or fewer.": "7d000f734447",
"Rinse the cup with clean water.": "dfdd8c289998",
"Start with water. Making a chip takes many steps with chemicals, and after these steps the wafer is rinsed. Tap water will not do. It carries minerals, tiny particles, and germs, and they would stay on the wafer when the water dried. Fabs use ultrapure water instead: water with almost everything removed except the water itself.": "882b1c01e3dc",
"Summer in Taiwan is hot and humid.": "dfcc97616211",
"The filter catches the dirt in the water.": "7cf7b1fac2a9",
"The machines need power too. The newest lithography machines, which print with extreme ultraviolet light, use about ten times as much electricity as the older kind. So the next time you hear that a fab needs a lot of water and power, you will know why. It is the price of being clean enough to build something so small.": "a01a34ff8a64",
"Tiny particles float in the air.": "a67deec919ec",
"Turn off the lights to save electricity.": "5ba478205a4c",
"Ultrapure water is made in stages. First the water is filtered. Then it is pushed through very fine membranes and special materials that pull out the dissolved minerals. Last comes a final polishing just before the water is used. A large modern fab uses several million gallons of this water every day.": "c1a6b0af2b0c",
"Water is precious, so fabs do not simply throw it away. Used water is collected, cleaned, and sent back to be used again. One chipmaker reports that its systems can reclaim more than 85 percent of the water used in making chips. Some fabs also make their ultrapure water from cleaned city wastewater instead of fresh water.": "92292d2e74be",
"We recycle paper and bottles at school.": "8b68508023dc",
"Why can't a fab rinse wafers with tap water?": "66d481666d7c",
"Why is dirt such a big problem in a fab?": "b38da5c1b067",
"Workers wear special suits in the cleanroom.": "526fed430897",
"You already know that the lines on a chip are measured in nanometers. That makes dust a giant. A particle only one fifth as wide as a line can ruin a chip. So the factory where chips are made, called a fab, has one great enemy: dirt. Almost everything unusual about a fab comes from the fight to stay clean.": "fbf9d6c8c914",
